    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0513" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.01/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-08T17:00:00+01:00">September 8,
                            1940—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 8—12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3039. The substance of your 2628, September 5, 8 p.m., has been communicated
                    orally to Admiral Muselier who appreciates the information given. He had
                    withheld his telegram pending receipt of your views and says that he will not
                    send it and will hold his hand until he believes that Martinique, Guadeloupe,
                    and French Guiana can be “converted” simultaneously. He reiterated his desire to
                    do nothing to which we would object.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
